      "document": {
        "_id": "EwZS3HoywMMJwnBZ",
        "name": "Worldscale Shield",
        "type": "shield",
        "system": {
          "publication": {
            "title": "Pathfinder #218: Titanbane",
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 8
          },
          "traits": {
            "value": ["magical", "mythic"],
            "rarity": "rare",
            "integrated": null
          },
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>It's believed that four <em>worldscale shields</em> (Hardness 9, HP 60, BT 30) exist, each made from the scale of one of the four worldscale serpents rumored to burrow through the heart of the world. When a hero-god went to slay one of these serpents, they found that they first needed to tear a scale from the beast's body to reveal the vulnerable flesh beneath. These four scales removed became the four <em>worldscale shields</em>.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Absorb Blow</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">f</span></p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You would take physical damage (bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing) from an attack and you have your <em>worldscale shield</em> Raised</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> Spend 1 Mythic Point. The <em>worldscale shield</em> completely absorbs the blow, preventing all damage that you would have taken from the attack. The <em>worldscale shield</em> breaks. If it was already broken, it is destroyed.</p>"
